/-! # ss-faltings: the chain of `sixContactMin_of_open76` rerouted off SGA 7 IX Cor. 3.3

The research field `sga7_IX_Cor3_3_Def34` (SGA 7 IX Cor. 3.3) and its descendants (`sga7_IX_Cor3_3`,
`sga7_IX_3_3_SHpre`, `sga7_IX_3_3_SH`, `sga7_IX_3_3`, `semistablePersistsSHcp`) are read only by height-split's SS1
(`SemistableReductionThm`, global form, through persistence), SS2 (`SemistableNeronBaseChange`) and SS3
(`SemistablePersists`), whose readers are the height rows R18, R19, R21, R22, `StableHeightFinite` and the lower half
of R20. On Faltings' route these need only `ZInQ.SSFaltings.FaltingsSemistableHeightBC` (Faltings 1983: the height of
a semistable abelian variety does not change under finite extension; used uncited at diophantine_zq.tex L596-598) and
`ZInQ.SSFaltings.SemistableReductionThmIF` (semistable over every field containing `K(A[15])`, proved from Raynaud's
criterion; `Contrib/OneProof/SSFaltings.lean`).

This module copies, verbatim up to the renaming `X ↦ X_sf` / `XSF`, every declaration of `sixContactMin_of_open76`'s proof that takes a
bundle carrying one of these fields (or an SS hypothesis), or reads one, with
* the Cor. 3.3 fields of a bundle replaced by one field `faltingsSemistableHeightBC : FaltingsSemistableHeightBC`;
* SS1 replaced by `semistableReductionThmIF : SemistableReductionThmIF`, SS2 by `faltingsSemistableHeightBC`, SS3
  dropped;
* `ss1_ss3_of14NF_hf_gm_pz_eb` replaced by `SSFaltings.semistableReductionThmIF_of_raynaud` (Raynaud's criterion from
  the same bundle fields as before, no persistence);
* the readers `heightRowsNo20_of8_hf_eb`, `r20Lower_of8_hf_eb` on SSFaltings' rows (`r18_of_leavesF`, …,
  `r20Lower_of_leavesF`).

Generated by `scratch/ss-faltings/gen/gen_chain.py`; never imports `ZInQKernel.OneProof.Main`. -/

